                  "When should my puppy or kitten be vaccinated?",
                  "The first vaccines usually start from around eight weeks, with boosters a few weeks apart. Bring any papers you have, and we will build a schedule for your pet."
                ],
                [
                  "How often do adult pets need vaccines?",
                  "Most adult dogs and cats need a yearly booster, and rabies follows the official schedule. We check your pet’s booklet and tell you what is due."
                ],
                [
                  "How should I prepare my pet for a visit?",
                  "Bring the vaccination booklet, keep cats in a carrier and dogs on a lead, and note appetite, drinking and behaviour. Ask us if your pet should skip a meal beforehand."
                ],
                [
                  "What should I do before surgery or a dental?",
                  "We give written instructions when you book: when to stop food and water, and what to bring. Following them keeps anaesthesia safe. If you are unsure, call the day before."
                ],
                [
                  "What counts as an emergency?",
                  "Trouble breathing, collapse, heavy bleeding, repeated vomiting, a swollen belly, seizures or a suspected poisoning. Call us straight away; if you cannot reach us, go to the nearest emergency clinic."
                ],
                [
                  "Do you groom nervous or elderly pets?",
                  "Yes. Tell us about fears, health problems or past bad experiences when you book. We take more time, short breaks and gentle handling."
